{"path":"/documentation/intervention/backends/remote","section":"documentation","title":"remote","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote","label":"remote","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteError","label":"RemoteError","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend","label":"RemoteBackend","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend","label":"AsyncRemoteBackend","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">remote</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Running a captured trace on a remote NDIF server.</p>\n<p>A trace captured locally can be shipped to NDIF and run against a model that\nnever leaves the server: the block is serialized source-and-all, POSTed, and the\nmodel is named by a <code>model_key</code> rather than pickled. The backends here differ\nonly in <em>how the client waits</em> for the job to finish and collect its saves:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a title=\"            RemoteBackend\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend\"><code>RemoteBackend</code></a> blocking -- one <code>/subscribe</code> websocket, streamed\n  status updates, result on COMPLETED (<code>model.trace(..., remote=True)</code>).</li>\n<li><a title=\"            RemoteBackend\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend\"><code>RemoteBackend</code></a> non-blocking (<code>blocking=False</code>) -- submit over HTTP\n  and poll the server's stored status until the result lands.</li>\n<li><a title=\"            AsyncRemoteBackend\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend\"><code>AsyncRemoteBackend</code></a> -- the blocking stream, awaited on an asyncio event\n  loop so a job runs without tying up a thread.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Status updates render through\n<a title=\"            StatusDisplay\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/backends/display#nnsight.intervention.backends.display.StatusDisplay\"><code>StatusDisplay</code></a>; a failed job\nsurfaces as <a title=\"            RemoteError\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteError\"><code>RemoteError</code></a>.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-object doc-class\">\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteError\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">RemoteError</span>\n\n\n</h3>\n\n\n    <div class=\"doc-contents\">\n            <p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><span title=\"Exception\">Exception</span></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>The remote job failed on the server.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    </div>\n\n</div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">RemoteBackend</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"RemoteBackend(model_key: str, host: Optional[str] = None, api_key: Optional[str] = None, env: Optional[dict] = None, blocking: bool = True, job_id: Optional[str] = None, verbose: bool = False)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><a title=\"            Backend (nnsight.tracing.backend.Backend)\" href=\"/documentation/tracing/backend#nnsight.tracing.backend.Backend\">Backend</a></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>Run a trace on a remote NDIF server, waiting for it in the calling thread.</p>\n<p>Serializes the captured block (the model is named by <code>model_key</code>, never\nserialized), ships it, and returns the saved values once the job finishes.\nTwo waiting modes, chosen by <code>blocking</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>blocking=True</code> (default): hold one <code>/subscribe</code> websocket open, stream\n  status updates until COMPLETED, then download the saves and push them back\n  into the caller's frame so its <code>h = ...save()</code> variables populate.</li>\n<li><code>blocking=False</code>: <a title=\"            submit\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.submit\"><code>submit</code></a> the job over plain HTTP (no websocket)\n  and store its <a title=\"            job_id\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.job_id\"><code>job_id</code></a>; the server records each status to the object\n  store, and each later call <a title=\"            poll\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.poll\"><code>poll</code></a>\\ s until the result is ready.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a title=\"            AsyncRemoteBackend\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend\"><code>AsyncRemoteBackend</code></a> runs the same blocking stream on an asyncio event\nloop instead.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.model_key\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">model_key</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"model_key = model_key"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.env\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">env</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"env = env or {}"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.blocking\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">blocking</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"blocking = blocking"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.job_id\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">job_id</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"job_id = job_id"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.status\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">status</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"status: Optional[Status] = None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.meta\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">meta</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"meta: Optional[dict] = None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.host\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">host</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"host = resolve_host(host)"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.api_key\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">api_key</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"api_key = api_key or CONFIG.API.APIKEY or ''"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.compress\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">compress</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"compress = CONFIG.API.COMPRESS"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.ws_host\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">ws_host</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"ws_host = ('wss' if scheme == 'https' else 'ws') + '://' + rest"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.verbose\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">verbose</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"verbose = verbose or CONFIG.APP.DEBUG"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.display\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">display</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"display = StatusDisplay(enabled=CONFIG.APP.REMOTE_LOGGING or self.verbose, verbose=self.verbose)"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.__call__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__call__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__call__(tracer: Optional[Tracer] = None) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.parse\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">parse</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-staticmethod\"><code>staticmethod</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"parse(message: Union[str, bytes]) -> ResponseModel"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Build a <a title=\"            ResponseModel\" href=\"/documentation/schema/response#nnsight.schema.response.ResponseModel\"><code>ResponseModel</code></a> from one websocket frame.</p>\n<p>A status update arrives as JSON in a text frame. A COMPLETED response\nmay instead arrive as a binary frame — <code>torch.save</code> bytes whose\n<code>data</code> is the result blob itself, sent when the server hands the\nresult back on the socket rather than staging it for download.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.note\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">note</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"note(response: ResponseModel) -> bool"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Render a status update, raise on ERROR, and report whether it's final.</p>\n<p>The shared status handling for every update, however it arrived (websocket,\npoll): update the display, raise <a title=\"            RemoteError\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteError\"><code>RemoteError</code></a> on ERROR, and return\nwhether the status is COMPLETED (so the caller knows to fetch the result).</p>\n<p>Also where <a title=\"            meta\n\n\n  \n      instance-attribute\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.meta\"><code>meta</code></a>\nis taken off the response, since every waiting mode but\n<a title=\"            stream\n\n\n  \n      async\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.stream\"><code>stream</code></a>\nreaches its result through here.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.handle\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">handle</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"handle(response: ResponseModel) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Process a single status update, returning the result on COMPLETED.</p>\n<p>Returns None for intermediate statuses. On COMPLETED <code>data</code> is either\nthe result blob itself — the server sent it back on the response — or a\npresigned url to download it from. Which one depends on the result's\nsize against the server's limit, so both have to be handled.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.download_result\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">download_result</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"download_result(url: Optional[str]) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Deserialize the result, downloading it first if it is not already here.</p>\n<p><code>url</code> is whatever COMPLETED carried: a presigned url to fetch, or the\nresult blob itself when the server sent it back on the response rather\nthan staging it. A url is downloaded in chunks behind a tqdm progress bar\n(shown when remote logging is enabled); either way the bytes go to\n<a title=\"            finalize\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.finalize\"><code>finalize</code></a>, which decompresses under the same flag the request\nwas compressed with and loads it with torch.load.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.finalize\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">finalize</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"finalize(content: bytes) -> RESULT"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Decompress (if the request was compressed) and load a result blob.</p>\n<p>The shared tail of every route the bytes can arrive by — downloaded from\na presigned url, or handed over on the response itself: everything after\nthe bytes are in hand.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.send\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">send</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"send(request: RequestModel, blob: bytes) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Submit the request and handle the initial (blocking) response.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.submit\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">submit</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"submit(tracer: Tracer) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Submit a non-blocking job: POST without a websocket and store the job id.</p>\n<p>No <code>/subscribe</code>, so the request carries no session id; the server saves\neach status response to the object store for <a title=\"            poll\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.poll\"><code>poll</code></a> to read. Returns\nNone — call <a title=\"            poll\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.poll\"><code>poll</code></a> (or the backend again) to fetch the result.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.poll\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">poll</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"poll(tracer: Optional[Tracer] = None) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Fetch the latest status of a submitted non-blocking job.</p>\n<p>GETs <code>/response/{job_id}</code>. Returns the saved-values dict on COMPLETED (the\ntrace has long since exited, so the caller reads it from the return rather\nthan from any frame), raises on ERROR, and returns None while the job is\nstill running (or before its first status lands). <code>status</code> holds the latest.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.request\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">request</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"request(request: RequestModel, tracer: Tracer) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">AsyncRemoteBackend</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"AsyncRemoteBackend(*args, **kwargs)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><a title=\"            RemoteBackend (nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend)\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend\">RemoteBackend</a></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>A <a title=\"            RemoteBackend\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend\"><code>RemoteBackend</code></a> whose waiting is async, over the same websocket.</p>\n<p><code>__call__</code> fires the request the way the blocking parent does — subscribe\nto the <code>/subscribe</code> websocket, take the session id, POST the payload — and\nreturns without consuming any status updates. That initial connection is\nsynchronous; only the waiting is async. Await the backend for the saves dict —\nwhich renders the status display and raises on a server error, like the blocking\nparent — or async-iterate it for the <em>raw</em> status updates to handle yourself,\nwith the saves dict yielded as the final item:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","code":"backend = AsyncRemoteBackend(model.to_model_key())\nwith model.trace(prompt, backend=backend):\n    out = model.output.save()\n\nresult = await backend                  # wait for COMPLETED, get the saves\n# or\nasync for update in backend:            # raw ResponseModel status updates...\n    if isinstance(update, dict):\n        result = update                 # ...and the saves dict, yielded last\n    else:\n        print(update.status)            # you decide what to do with each"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>The websocket <code>recv</code> is blocking, so <a title=\"            receive\n\n\n  \n      async\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.receive\"><code>receive</code></a> runs it through\n<code>asyncio.to_thread</code> to keep the event loop free while a job runs. Only\nthat waiting differs from the parent — the connect, serialization, POST, and the\ndecompress/load reuse the parent's synchronous methods.</p>\n<p>The caller's frame is gone by the time the result lands (the trace has exited),\nso — like the parent's non-blocking path — the saved values aren't pushed back\ninto it; they come out of the await / the iterator's final item.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.connection\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">connection</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"connection: Optional[object] = None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.__call__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__call__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__call__(tracer: Optional[Tracer] = None) -> 'AsyncRemoteBackend'"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.__await__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__await__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__await__()"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.resolve\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">resolve</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"resolve() -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Consume status updates until COMPLETED, returning the saves dict.</p>\n<p>The trace has exited, so — like the non-blocking poll — nothing is pushed\nback into a frame; the caller reads the returned dict.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.__aiter__\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">__aiter__</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"__aiter__() -> AsyncIterator[Any]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.stream\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">stream</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"stream() -> AsyncIterator[Any]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Yield each raw status update as it lands, then the saves dict last.</p>\n<p>Unlike <a title=\"            resolve\n\n\n  \n      async\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.resolve\"><code>resolve</code></a>, this doesn't touch the display or raise on ERROR —\nit hands you each <a title=\"            ResponseModel\" href=\"/documentation/schema/response#nnsight.schema.response.ResponseModel\"><code>ResponseModel</code></a> as-is to do with as you like. The\nfinal item (after COMPLETED) is the downloaded saves dict; an ERROR update\njust ends the stream (inspect it and raise yourself if you want).</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.receive\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">receive</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"receive() -> ResponseModel"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Await the next status update off the websocket (blocking recv in a thread).</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.download\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">download</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-async\"><code>async</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"download(url: Optional[str]) -> Optional[RESULT]"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Async <a title=\"            download_result\" href=\"#nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.RemoteBackend.download_result\"><code>download_result</code></a>: stream the blob with an async client, then\nhand it to the parent's shared decompress/load.</p>\n<p><code>url</code> is whatever COMPLETED carried: a presigned url to fetch, or the\nresult blob itself when the server sent it back on the response. Both\n<code>resolve</code> and <code>stream</code> reach the result through here rather than through\n<code>handle</code>, so the bytes case is answered here too.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.intervention.backends.remote.AsyncRemoteBackend.close\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">close</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"close() -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Close the subscription websocket (idempotent).</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}